// Guide
"c100_guide_basic_header" = "Basics";
"c100_guide_bt_pairing_mode_p1" = "When the glasses are powered on for the first time, they will automatically enter Bluetooth pairing mode.\n\nAlternatively, press the \"Function Button\" 7 times consecutively to unpair current Bluetooth. The inner indicator light will flash blue, indicating it has entered Bluetooth pairing mode.";
"c100_guide_bt_pairing_mode_title" = "How to enter Bluetooth pairing mode?";
"c100_guide_device_not_found_p1" = "When the App cannot find the glasses, please troubleshoot with the following steps:\nI. Basic Check and Operation\n\n1. Open phone system Bluetooth list:\nGo to system Bluetooth settings, find and remove glasses named 【INMO Moment Max】+ 4-digit code in history, select and tap 【Forget This Device】.\n\n2. Glasses actively clear binding record:\nWhile not wearing the glasses, press the \"Function Button\" 7 times consecutively to unpair current Bluetooth until the inner indicator light turns solid blue. After a moment, the inner indicator light flashes blue, indicating the glasses are entering pairing mode.\n\n3. Actively connect:\nOpen phone system Bluetooth settings, find the glasses named 【INMO Moment Max】+ 4-digit code in the Bluetooth list, and tap to connect.\n\nII. Restore Factory Settings\nIf basic checks do not resolve the issue, please try the following:\nRestore factory settings (Please proceed with caution):\nImportant Note: This operation will lose all unsynced video and audio recordings in the glasses.\nSteps: While not wearing the glasses, press and hold both the \"Power Button\" and \"Capture Button\" for 5 seconds until the inner indicator light flashes red, indicating factory reset has started.\nWait for 1-3 minutes. When the inner indicator light turns solid white for 2 seconds, factory reset is complete. The glasses will then reboot and enter Bluetooth pairing mode. After reset is complete, try pairing again.";
"c100_guide_device_not_found_title" = "INMO Moment APP cannot find the device?";
"c100_guide_factory_reset_detail_title" = "How to reset the glasses (restore factory settings)?";
"c100_guide_factory_reset_p1" = "While not wearing the glasses, press and hold both the \"Power Button\" and \"Capture Button\" for 5 seconds until the inner indicator light flashes red, indicating factory reset has started.\n\nWait for 1-3 minutes. When the inner indicator light turns solid white for 2 seconds, factory reset is complete. The glasses will then reboot and enter Bluetooth pairing mode.";
"c100_guide_factory_reset_title" = "How to restore factory settings";
"c100_guide_firmware_ota_p1" = "When a new version is available, you can start the update via:\n\n1. Open INMO Moment App, go to \"Settings\" page, select \"About Glasses\", then tap \"Firmware Update\". Follow the on-screen instructions to complete the update.\n\n2. When firmware requires a mandatory update, tap the update prompt directly on the \"Home\" or \"Glasses\" page of INMO Moment App.\n\nA normal glasses update takes 6-10 minutes. Before updating, the inner indicator light turns white. During updating, the inner indicator light will turn off until reboot succeeds, after which it stays solid white for 4 seconds. Note: ensure the glasses battery is above 20% before updating.";
"c100_guide_firmware_ota_title" = "How to update glasses firmware?";
"c100_guide_first_pair_p1" = "Please ensure your phone's Bluetooth is turned on, and INMO Moment App has been granted Bluetooth and network permissions.\n\nWhile not wearing the glasses, press and hold the \"Power Button\" for 3 seconds until the inner indicator light flashes blue, indicating the glasses have entered Bluetooth pairing mode.\n\nOpen INMO Moment App, go to \"Choose Product\" page, select \"inmo Moment Max\", and follow the on-screen instructions to search and pair.";
"c100_guide_first_pair_title" = "How to pair and connect the glasses with the App for the first time?";
